course: dictionary
lesson: 2533
title: Deep: how far down, how low, how strong
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word deep has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one. In «the deep sea is full of strange animals», deep means far down from the top. In «a deep voice», it means low. In «deep feelings», it means strong.
explain: Look at the words near deep. In «Take a deep breath», deep means a big, full breath. In «the pool is two metres deep», deep tells you how far down the water goes. Ask yourself: which meaning fits here?
explain: Deep is an adjective, so it can change to deeper and deepest to compare things: a deeper pool has more water going further down than a shallow one. Deep can also be an adverb, as in «The diver went deep».
fact: Deep means going far down from the top, as in a deep pool.
fact: Deep can also tell how far down something goes: «2 metres deep».
fact: A deep sound is low, and a deep colour is dark and strong.
fact: «A deep sleep» is hard to wake from, and «deep feelings» are strong.
fact: The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish, at over eight kilometres down.
exercise: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» In this sentence, what does deepest mean? | Most tired | Darkest in colour | Loudest | *Going furthest down from the top
exercise: Mia says, «The pool is two metres deep.» What does deep tell us? | *How far down the water goes | How loud the water sounds | How much the pool costs | How dark the water is
exercise: «Horses can sleep standing up, though they still lie down for short times for deep sleep.» What does deep sleep mean? | A short nap on the grass | A sleep standing up | *A sleep that is hard to wake from | A sleep with a deep voice
test: «He gave a deep, low laugh.» Which meaning of deep fits best? | A hole going far down | A pale colour | Very tired | *A sound that is low
test: «Her deep feelings showed in her letter.» What does deep mean here? | Low | *Strong | Dark-coloured | Far down
exam: «Vent water can be hotter than three hundred degrees, but it does not boil because of the huge pressure of the deep sea.» What does deep sea mean here? | A sea with strong feelings | A sea with a low, booming sound | *The sea far down below the surface | A sea that is very shallow
